st destination in Texas. In 2018, bizjournals.com ranked Fort Worth the 7th most affordable city to live and work in the United States and U.S. News and World Report named Fort Worth one of the Best Places to Live. Fort Worth, Dallas and Arlington all rank among the top 25 most diverse cities in the country. Fort Worth is known for its vast array of cultural, educational and entertainment opportunities. The city boasts three world class art museums\u2014the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall is one of the premier performance venues in the country. Concerts, film festivals and other events are held regularly at Sundance Square, Panther Island and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: TCU only accepts online applications and documents. To apply for a part-time adjunct position, attach a letter of application and a curriculum vita to the online application. Additional documents may be required by the department at a later time. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert f07e2e47 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Temporary Temporary First Name (required) 39a0d490 Last Name (required) 9719a5d6 Email (required) c0cf4a69 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 30ee79f2 Last Name (required) 97828cb7 Email (required) 6f754c17 Who would you like to share this with? 10835daf Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) ad4825ea Last Name (required) 027d6936 Email (required) 4f33a1a2 Resume 16de341d Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 01edbb96 Last Name (required) b297df11 Email (required) 62eed6d8 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 036e96de Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply bbb326a3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/arts-leadership-and-entrepreneurship-faculty-adjunct-pool-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-b59697a8-6874-4b40-928a-5bbcae19150e": {"title": "Arts Leadership and Entrepreneurship Faculty Adjunct Pool", "description": "Arts Leadership and Entrepreneurship Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Arts Leadership and Entrepreneurship Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Arts Leadership and Entrepreneurship Faculty Adjunct Pool College of Fine Arts Apply Now Arts Leadership and Entrepreneurship Faculty Adjunct Pool 499435 Adjunct Faculty Temporary Opening on: Apr 1 2024 College of Fine Arts Application Deadline: Not applicable Position Details: The Arts Leadership and Entrepreneurship program in the College of Fine Arts occasionally has openings for part-time temporary adjunct instructors. Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in arts leadership and entrepreneurship would add the applicant to a pool which is available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. Department Details: N/A School/College Description: The TCU College of Fine Arts is home to six academic units: the School of Art, the School for Classical & Contemporary Dance, the School of Music, the Department of Design, the Department of Fashion Merchandising, and the Department of Theatre. The college is comprised of approximately 1000 students and offers 33 undergraduate degree programs and 24 advanced degree programs to prepare the next generation of creative leaders in the arts. Students in the College of Fine Arts study with renowned professors and guest artists, annually present more than 350 public performances and display art, design, and research in juried exhibitions and competitions. The college also offers a minor and certificate in Arts Leadership & Entrepreneurship and oversees two on-campus art galleries. University & Fort Worth Description: ABOUT TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University sits on 302 acres nestled in a primarily residential part of Fort Worth, just minutes away from downtown. The University includes seven schools and colleges, in addition to the John V. Roach Honors College and the Burnett School of Medicine. Currently, TCU enrolls more than 10,200 undergraduates and 1,700 graduate students. Twenty-eight percent of students self-identify as a member of a minority group, five percent are international students, and forty-five percent are from out-of-state. Our students are supported by more than 2,200 faculty and staff. The University has more than 700 full-time faculty members and is a top 100 National University as classified by US News and World Report and has a Carnegie Classification of R2: Doctoral Universities \u2013 High Research Activity. ABOUT FORT WORTH Like TCU, Fort Worth has the approachable, friendly charm of a smaller town, but offers the amenities, cultural activities, diversity and unique personality of a much larger city. Fort Worth, Texas, is the 13th largest city in the United States with an ever-growing population nearing 1 million. Fort Worth and TCU have grown together in a nearly 150-year relationship. You\u2019ll find that many Horned Frogs remain here after graduation, thanks to the region\u2019s thriving job market. Fort Worth is part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area, the fourth largest metropolitan area in the United States, and the number 1 tourist destination in Texas. In 2018, bizjournals.com ranked Fort Worth the 7th most affordable city to live and work in the United States and U.S. News and World Report named Fort Worth one of the Best Places to Live. Fort Worth, Dallas and Arlington all rank among the top 25 most diverse cities in the country. Fort Worth is known for its vast array of cultural, educational and entertainment opportunities. The city boasts three world class art museums\u2014the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall is one of the premier performance venues in the country. Concerts, film festivals and other events are held regularly at Sundance Square, Panther Island and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: TCU only accepts online applications and documents. To apply for a part-time adjunct position, attach a letter of application and a curriculum vita to the online application. Additional documents may be required by the department at a later time. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert d42af757 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Temporary Temporary First Name (required) 98cb7343 Last Name (required) b05ab188 Email (required) 667c487a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 1dd8a649 Last Name (required) eb3e2726 Email (required) 03312cdc Who would you like to share this with? 0ee8006e Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 28b6e9b5 Last Name (required) 21d5664a Email (required) 5b633e83 Resume bc8aa5a3 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 8ce6e19d Last Name (required) a1cf763b Email (required) 82a60c6f What type of job are you looking for? (required) cefb559c Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 91bc05a7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-economics-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-ac05301b-54f7-4e64-9e48-319fa6803cd2": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics AddRan College Apply Now Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics 500990 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 14 2026 AddRan College Application Deadline: November, 15th 2026 Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on campus and in person. The Department of Economics at Texas Christian University (TCU) invites applications for a tenure-track position at either the Assistant or Associate Professor level as part of a cluster hire beginning August 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute in the area of quantitative economics, with demonstrated research expertise in machine learning and/or artificial intelligence methods, and to teach at the undergraduate and Master\u2019s levels. All Ph.D. requirements should be complete by August 2027. Departmental representatives will conduct virtual interviews. Finalists will be invited to campus for in-person visits. Department Details: TCU is a private research university, and the Department of Economics is part of the AddRan College of Liberal Arts that emphasizes the ideals of a liberal arts education and a teacher-scholar model with a 3/2 course load. Students are encouraged to explore alternative points of view and to develop the tools necessary for independent analysis. We place a strong value on excellence in teaching, research and mentoring. The department serves approximately 350 majors across four undergraduate degrees (BA, BS, BS in International Economics, and BS in Economics & Mathematics) and will offer a Master of Science in Economics with Quantitative and AI Methods (MSEQAI) starting summer 2027. School/College Description: Named for TCU\u2019s founders, Addison and Randolph Clark, the AddRan College of Liberal Arts is home to the core academic disciplines of the humanities and social sciences. The College includes approximately 155 full-time faculty members, 13 departments (Comparative Race & Ethnic Studies, Criminology & Criminal Justice, Economics, English, Geography, History, Modern Language Studies, Philosophy, Political Science, Religion, Sociology & Anthropology, Spanish and Hispanic Studies, and Women & Gender Studies), and two units of Reserve Officers\u2019 Training Corps (Army and Air Force). AddRan College departments confer 17 Bachelor of Arts and 7 Bachelor of Science degrees, a Bachelor of General Studies, an online master\u2019s degree in Criminology and Criminal Justice, a Master of Liberal Arts degree, and master\u2019s and Ph.D. degrees in History, English, and Rhetoric and Composition. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: By November 15, interested individuals should upload 1) a cover letter, 2) CV, 3) job market paper, 4) statement regarding research plans, and 5) evidence of effective teaching, including details on classroom experience. At least three confidential letters of recommendation which should be sent via the AEA JOE system by November 15. The application will be considered incomplete and not evaluated if at least three letters are not submitted by the deadline. TCU only accepts online applications and documents. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert e4618a56 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) 382e8d38 Last Name (required) 7d20e6dc Email (required) c1c2254e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 263af1a1 Last Name (required) 61dc5f89 Email (required) 120a3d01 Who would you like to share this with? 25cbe876 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 7ad60419 Last Name (required) e8c136b4 Email (required) 9591646e Resume e1fe4c28 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) dfa11d23 Last Name (required) 113ad842 Email (required) fee9fa67 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 5169fc10 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply a5f81b66 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-professional-practice-in-computer-science-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Practice in Computer Science", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Practice in Computer Science - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Practice in Computer Science - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Practice in Computer Science College of Science & Engineering Apply Now Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Practice in Computer Science 501325 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 28 2026 Closing on: Nov 30 2026 College of Science & Engineering Application Deadline: November 30, 2026 Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of Computer Science at Texas Christian University invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Practice faculty position. The successful candidate will join a department committed to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education and to preparing students for careers in computing and related fields. Candidates must possess a master's degree in computer science or a closely related field. A Ph.D. in computer science is preferred. Candidates should have relevant professional, industry, or academic experience in computing or a closely related field and demonstrate an interest in bringing practical and contemporary perspectives into the classroom. The Department is particularly interested in candidates with expertise in computer systems, cybersecurity, or software engineering. However, outstanding candidates from any sub-discipline of computer science are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate should have broad interests in computing and be prepared to teach undergraduate courses at multiple levels. Depending upon the candidate's expertise and departmental needs, teaching responsibilities may include courses in programming and software development, computer systems, operating systems, computer networks, cybersecurity, software engineering, and other areas of computer science. The position is primarily teaching-focused and includes service to the Department, College, and University. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to curriculum development, student advising and mentoring, undergraduate projects, and other departmental activities. Opportunities may also exist to participate in graduate education and activities associated with the Department's Ph.D. program in Computer Science. Candidates who can contribute to the Department's applied computing curriculum and who have experience with current technologies, development environments, and professional practices are particularly encouraged to apply. Appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Practice level will be determined based on the successful candidate's qualifications and professional and teaching experience. Department Details: The Department of Computer Science at Texas Christian University is housed within the Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering and has approximately 220 students and nine full-time faculty members. The Department supports academic programs in Computer Science, Computer Information Technology, and Data Science, and offers a Ph.D. program in Computer Science. The Department is committed to providing students with a strong foundation in the principles of computing while also offering opportunities to gain practical experience with contemporary computing technologies. Its curriculum encompasses areas including programming, algorithms and data structures, computer systems, operating systems, computer networks, cybersecurity, databases, software engineering, artificial intelligence, data science, cloud computing, and parallel and high-performance computing. Faculty members are committed to excellence in teaching and work closely with students through coursework, advising, independent study, research, and project-based learning. The Department values close faculty-student interaction and provides opportunities for students to apply their knowledge through research, internships, senior design, and other project experiences. TCU's location in the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area provides significant opportunities for engagement with a large and diverse technology community. The region is home to major employers in software, aerospace and defense, telecommunications, finance, healthcare, transportation, consulting, and information technology, providing opportunities for industry collaboration, internships, and student employment. School/College Description: The Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering encompasses 9 departments (Biology, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Computer Science, Engineering, Environmental and Geological Sciences, Mathematics, Nutritional Sciences, Physics & Astronomy, and Psychology) as well as the Ranch Management Program, which offers both an undergraduate degree and a one-year certificate program. Davis College is also home to the Pre-Health Professions Institute, the Karyn Purvis Institute for Child Development, the Institute of Behavioral Research, the Institute for Environmental Studies, Monnig Meteorite Gallery, and the Institute for Ranch Management. Davis College is the second largest at TCU in terms of both undergraduate enrollment and number of majors. It contains a disproportionate percentage of high-achieving students, as evidenced by the fact that almost one-half of the students in the Honors College have majors in The Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering. Research opportunities abound for undergraduates, with 46 percent of majors engaging in a substantive experience during which they work one-on-one with their faculty mentor. Davis College also has five doctoral programs and 16 master\u2019s programs, as well as two graduate certificate programs. Davis College faculty are true teacher-scholars, for whom instruction and research are viewed as complementary activities. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Applicants should submit the following materials electronically: \u2022 Curriculum vitae or r\u00e9sum\u00e9; \u2022 Cover letter describing the candidate's qualifications and interest in the position; \u2022 Statement of teaching philosophy and teaching interests. The statement should identify courses in the Department's current curriculum that the candidate would be prepared to teach. A list of courses is available on the Department of Computer Science website (https://cse.tcu.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/course-information.php); and \u2022 Contact information for three professional references. Letters of recommendation will be requested only for finalists. Applicants are encouraged to describe relevant industry, professional, or academic experience and how that experience would contribute to undergraduate teaching and student preparation for careers in computing. For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Michael Scherger Search Committee Chair, Department of Computer Science Email: m.scherger@tcu.edu Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert c69e4257 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) b08f049c Last Name (required) 118fa15d Email (required) 213d6b2e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 56f43bef Last Name (required) 65d92ad7 Email (required) dcd922b9 Who would you like to share this with? 07e4a508 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 84d51167 Last Name (required) 7dba11d2 Email (required) a9206574 Resume c848b9eb Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 3c60b9c8 Last Name (required) 08b6a9b0 Email (required) a7cea899 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 1a958985 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 7cfc44cf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-accounting-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting", "description": "Assistant Professor of Accounting - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Accounting - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Accounting M.J. Neeley School of Business Apply Now Assistant Professor of Accounting 501050 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Jun 29 2026 M.J. Neeley School of Business Application Deadline: September 1, 2026 Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of Accounting at Texas Christian University invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Accounting in the Neeley School of Business for Fall 2027. Teaching responsibilities include undergraduate and graduate courses. This is an in-person, on-campus position. The Neeley School supports and expects high quality research. Successful candidates will demonstrate the potential to publish in leading accounting journals. Apply by September 1, 2026 for full consideration; the position will remain open until filled. Department Details: The Department of Accounting includes 25 faculty and 2 administrative staff who work together in a highly collegial manner. The department offers AACSB-accredited BBA and MAc degrees, in addition to supporting the Neeley School's other BBA, MBA, and MS degree programs. Faculty provide an outstanding education and classroom experience for TCU students and actively engage in research that is published in top journals. School/College Description: The nationally ranked TCU Neeley School of Business has more than 3,500 students enrolled across undergraduate and graduate programs, with approximately one third of TCU students in its programs as majors, minors or advanced degree seekers. Departments include Accounting, Business Information Systems, Entrepreneurship and Innovation, Finance, Management and Leadership, Marketing and Supply and Value Chain Management, as well as seven graduate programs including full-time, part-time and online MBA and MS degrees. The Neeley School was ranked No. 9 in the nation and No. 1 in Texas for highest starting salaries for undergraduates in 2022 (Poets&Quants, 2022). The school\u2019s BBA is ranked #25 Best Undergraduate program in 2024, and was named one of the top 10 Undergraduate Business Schools to Watch (Poets&Quants, 2022). The Neeley School has the No. 36 ranked Full-time MBA in the U.S., and is No. 8 for Learning, No. 24 for Entrepreneurship, and No. 32 for Networking (Bloomberg Businessweek, 2024). The Neeley School is committed to fostering an inclusive, scholarly community composed of individuals who, through their diverse and sometimes competing perspectives, contribute to a free and intellectually challenging culture where students, faculty, staff and alumni have equitable opportunities and can forge paths toward personal and professional growth. We build upon the momentum generated by living the Neeley Promise: The Neeley School of Business unleashes human potential with leadership at the core and innovation in our spirit. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: All applications must be submitted electronically through the TCU HR system at https://jobs.tcu.edu. From this page, you can search for this position by the title \u201cAssistant Professor of Accounting.\u201d Alternatively, under \"Jobs by Category\u201d select \"Neeley School of Business\" to find this position among a listing of all business school positions. Applicants should submit the following to the online application: (1) a cover letter, (2) a CV, (3) evidence of high-quality scholarly activity and potential, including one working paper, and (4) three references with addresses, email addresses, and phone numbers. Candidates may submit evidence of teaching excellence or potential. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 6ce58712 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) ec4aaaeb Last Name (required) 26c8a048 Email (required) 1e4ea585 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 742096af Last Name (required) 9a85f2cb Email (required) 751f1687 Who would you like to share this with? ebd941c2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 7c254770 Last Name (required) 58db87a5 Email (required) 38e54943 Resume b2edff91 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 36da3f9e Last Name (required) 2ec2c185 Email (required) 2ce04c08 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 42732ec1 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 9784e2b1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-computer-science-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Computer Science", "description": "Assistant Professor of Computer Science - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Computer Science - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Computer Science College of Science & Engineering Apply Now Assistant Professor of Computer Science 501304 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 17 2026 College of Science & Engineering Application Deadline: Open until filled. Review of applications will begin November 13, 2026. Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of Computer Science at Texas Christian University (TCU) invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions beginning in Fall 2027. As TCU advances toward Carnegie R1 status, we seek colleagues who will strengthen the department's research profile while contributing to our tradition of excellence in teaching and student mentorship. Successful candidates will demonstrate strong potential to establish an impactful, externally funded research program and a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring students at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Applicants from all areas of computer science are encouraged to apply. Areas of particular interest include Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity and Privacy, Quantum and Advanced Computing, and Cyber-Physical and Autonomous Systems. We especially welcome candidates whose research addresses significant scientific, technological, or societal challenges and creates opportunities for interdisciplinary and externally funded research. Applications received by November 13, 2026, will receive full consideration. Review of applications will begin immediately thereafter and continue until the positions are filled. Qualifications Required: \u2022 Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field by August 1, 2027. \u2022 Strong potential for impactful research and scholarly contributions. \u2022 Demonstrated potential to develop and sustain an externally funded research program. \u2022 Commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring students at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. \u2022 Interest in contributing to the continued growth of the department and its graduate programs. Preferred: \u2022 Research expertise in an area that complements or expands the department's existing strengths. \u2022 Experience with proposal development or evidence of success in securing external research funding. \u2022 Potential to develop a nationally recognized research program. \u2022 Interest in interdisciplinary and collaborative research. Department Details: The Department of Computer Science offers a collaborative and collegial environment, a highly motivated student body, and strong support for both teaching and research. The department is experiencing significant growth in faculty, research, and graduate education, with 9 tenure-track/tenured faculty members and more than 200 undergraduate majors. Our Ph.D. program in Computer Science welcomed its inaugural cohort of nine fully funded doctoral students in Fall 2026, creating new opportunities for graduate education, research, and doctoral student mentorship. Faculty conduct research across a broad range of areas, including artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, data science, software engineering, computer systems, and emerging computing technologies. Faculty benefit from competitive startup packages, research computing infrastructure, and strong institutional support for pursuing external funding and interdisciplinary research. The department offers substantial opportunities for collaboration across TCU and with external partners. TCU\u2019s location in the Dallas-Fort Worth metroplex provides access to a vibrant technology ecosystem and opportunities for industry partnerships, internships, sponsored projects, and applied research collaborations. We seek colleagues who are excited to contribute to a growing and ambitious department through impactful research, excellent teaching, student mentorship, and collaborative engagement. School/College Description: The Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering encompasses 9 departments (Biology, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Computer Science, Engineering, Environmental and Geological Sciences, Mathematics, Nutritional Sciences, Physics & Astronomy, and Psychology) as well as the Ranch Management Program, which offers both an undergraduate degree and a one-year certificate program. Davis College is also home to the Pre-Health Professions Institute, the Karyn Purvis Institute for Child Development, the Institute of Behavioral Research, the Institute for Environmental Studies, Monnig Meteorite Gallery, and the Institute for Ranch Management. Davis College is the second largest at TCU in terms of both undergraduate enrollment and number of majors. It contains a disproportionate percentage of high-achieving students, as evidenced by the fact that almost one-half of the students in the Honors College have majors in The Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering. Research opportunities abound for undergraduates, with 46 percent of majors engaging in a substantive experience during which they work one-on-one with their faculty mentor. Davis College also has five doctoral programs and 16 master\u2019s programs, as well as two graduate certificate programs. Davis College faculty are true teacher-scholars, for whom instruction and research are viewed as complementary activities. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Interested candidates should submit the following: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Research statement 4. Teaching statement 5. Contact information for three references (letters will be requested for finalists) In your materials, please address how your research, teaching, and service will contribute to TCU's strategic goal of achieving Carnegie R1 classification. Highlight how your work will: \u2022 Advance impactful scholarship \u2022 Secure external funding \u2022 Foster interdisciplinary collaboration Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 5bb2b8ce Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) bf3691b9 Last Name (required) 8904c22d Email (required) c038238d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 2e2759ee Last Name (required) 7f77376e Email (required) 8d40e3c4 Who would you like to share this with? a8f1a085 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) d94d4396 Last Name (required) e2803e9c Email (required) dc74f55d Resume e0cc4802 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 21517912 Last Name (required) 5922c6c4 Email (required) 59fa7900 What type of job are you looking for? (required) b28a315f Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 27ff4a67 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-counseling-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Counseling", "description": "Assistant Professor of Counseling - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Counseling - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Counseling College of Education Apply Now Assistant Professor of Counseling 501288 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 17 2026 College of Education Application Deadline: Position will be open until filled. Review of Applications will begin October 12, 2026 Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Counseling program at Texas Christian University (TCU) invites applications for appointment as a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Counseling, beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will teach and advise students in the clinical mental health counseling specialization both at the master's and doctoral levels. TCU strives toward inclusive excellence and encourages applications from members of underrepresented groups. The successful candidate for this position will have strong potential for or a demonstrated track record of research excellence focused broadly on counselor development, multicultural counseling, and clinical mental health counseling outcomes. We are especially interested in scholars pursuing research in areas such as addictions, abnormal human behavior, military veteran support, play therapy, LGBTQIA+ communities, and/or interpersonal neurobiology. We expect the successful candidate to have the potential for, or a strong record of, securing external grants to support their research program at a level sufficient to ensure the impact of their work. Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include teaching, research/scholarship, advising, professional development, and service commensurate with the rank of Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will align all coursework to CACREP standards. The successful candidate will: \u25cf Teach counseling master\u2019s and doctoral-level courses, potentially including addictions, abnormal behavior, assessment, research and program evaluation, play therapy, and/or other content as needed. \u25cf Assist in program services such as program coordination and/or CACREP accreditation. \u25cf Advise, mentor, and chair master's- and doctoral-level students, including serving on orals/comprehensive examination, dissertation committees, and eventually chairing dissertations \u25cf Maintain a robust line of research and publication \u25cf Have the potential for or a strong record of securing external grants to support their program of research \u25cf Collaborate with counseling faculty on student recruitment, assessment, and retention; program evaluation; and support for the TCU community counseling training centers (Frog Care Centers). \u25cf Provide service to the college, department, university, and counseling-related professional organizations. Required Qualifications: \u25cf Earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program. ABD candidates will be considered but must complete degree requirements by appointment date. \u25cf Established research agenda as evidenced by publications or other recognized scholarly outlets \u25cf Eligible for LPC in Texas. \u25cf Ability to teach courses across the CACREP curriculum \u25cf Ability to teach, mentor, and conduct research that reflects awareness of and responsiveness to individual differences among students and clients. Preferred Qualifications: \u25cf Experience teaching doctoral-level classes \u25cf Three or more years of clinical experience in mental health or in school-based mental health services \u25cf Experience with program coordination and/or CACREP accreditation process \u25cf Supervision credentials (i.e., LPC-S in Texas, NBCC Approved Clinical Supervisor) \u25cf Experience securing external funding and grant writing. \u25cf Scholarship and experience with intervention studies or other quantitative methodologies. Department Details: The Counseling program takes a collaborative approach to counseling, viewing clients as active participants in their own growth and understanding rather than passive recipients of a diagnostic process.The Counseling program is housed in the Department of Counseling, Societal Change, and Inquiry. Programs in this department engage students looking to positively impact society in several ways, including addressing mental health through counseling, investigating the relationships between curriculum in schools and society, and working with youth in organizations connected to education. School/College Description: TCU\u2019s College of Education provides exceptional preparation for the most inspired and inspiring educators, counselors, leaders, and youth advocates. The college offers both B.S. and B.S.E. degrees at the undergraduate level, as well as five master's programs and five doctoral programs, many of which are nationally recognized. Programs include eighteen content area pathways to teacher certification in K -12 education along with programs and/or concentrations in youth advocacy, early intervention, bilingual education, English as a Second Language (ESL), curriculum and instruction, curriculum studies, counseling and counselor education, educational leadership, higher education leadership, science education, mathematics education, language and literacy education, and special education. TCU is the only university in the nation with two on-campus laboratory schools, Starpoint and KinderFrogs, for children with learning differences. Students have the opportunity to engage in real-world experiences with our centers, institutes, programs, and community partners. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Applicants should submit: (1) one- to two-page cover letter that addresses required qualifications; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) one-page statement of teaching philosophy; (4) one- to two-page statement of research; and (5) contact details (name, affiliation, e-mail address, and phone number) for three references. TCU uses an online application protocol administered by Human Resources. All application materials must be submitted electronically at: https://jobs.tcu.edu. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 93684383 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) 15ca466e Last Name (required) ed6daca7 Email (required) a3be7e0e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 74c53b77 Last Name (required) f756baed Email (required) c837cb71 Who would you like to share this with? 72fe5e7d Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4caa8d51 Last Name (required) 02ba562e Email (required) a459580e Resume 59a81a8c Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 07f3e25a Last Name (required) 3cf2a90e Email (required) 73c7551c What type of job are you looking for? (required) ce367f6f Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply d3994dc9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-dance-in-the-college-of-fine-arts-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Dance in the College of Fine Arts", "description": "Assistant Professor of Dance in the College of Fine Arts - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Dance in the College of Fine Arts - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Dance in the College of Fine Arts College of Fine Arts Apply Now Assistant Professor of Dance in the College of Fine Arts 501265 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 8 2026 College of Fine Arts Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Position Details: Qualifications and Experience This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The School for Classical & Contemporary Dance (SCCDance) in the College of Fine Arts at Texas Christian University invites applications for the position Assistant Professor of Dance to teach contemporary dance technique and related courses. The SCCDance seeks candidates who are experienced, committed, engaged, and passionate artist-educators who will provide a balance of expertise with current faculty members. This is a full time on-campus tenure-track faculty position. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty, dedicated staff, and motivated students in a community of artist-scholars and a culture defined by care and excellence. The start date of the position is August 2027. Required: \u2022 Terminal degree in Dance or related area; or with degree completion expected by start date; or MA with minimum seven (7) years of professional performing/teaching experience in Dance. \u2022 Minimum three (3) years pre-professional teaching experience. \u2022 Evidence of creative or scholarly research activity, and/or trajectory, consistent with tenure track expectations. Preferred: \u2022 Experience teaching at the university or college level in dance and related courses. \u2022 Experience teaching a diasporic or culturally rooted dance form, including but not limited to: West-African, hip-hop, house, folkl\u00f3rico, Gaga, Dunham, t\u00e9cnica cubana, Butoh, Bollywood, etc. \u2022 Experience teaching classroom-based courses in dance (theory, history, teaching methods, anatomy, etc.). Department Details: School for Classical & Contemporary Dance The School for Classical & Contemporary Dance (SCCDance) was founded in 1949 and offers three BFA degrees dedicated to conservatory-style depth inside a liberal arts education. DanceTCU offers seven distinct productions each academic year, welcomes numerous guest artists, collaborates across disciplines, and pursues unique opportunities that support student professional and educational development. SCCDance alumni are performers, choreographers, artistic directors, arts administrators, educators, program developers, studio owners, designers, dance therapists, dance photographers, and more. They also take their TCU education into prestigious graduate programs and fields such as medicine, physical therapy, counseling, journalism, and law. With a mission to develop educated dance artists prepared to become ethical professionals and leaders in the global dance community, the SCCDance is committed to preparing students to enter the field of dance and beyond. Texas Christian University\u2019s School for Classical & Contemporary Dance offers conservatory-style dance programs in a rigorous academic setting. It houses a community of artist-scholars dedicated to valuing each individual\u2019s unique pathway through the BFA. The SCCDance faculty provides opportunities and experiences to support student growth: artistically, intellectually, creatively, and collaboratively. Whether in the studio, on the stage, or in the classroom, a BFA from the SCCDance prepares students with essential skills in dance and beyond. TCU is accredited by the National Association of Schools of Dance (NASD). Admission to the TCU SCCDance is highly competitive. Students must apply to the university through the Office of Undergraduate Admission and to the SCCDance. An audition for the SCCDance is required. The SCCDance offers a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Ballet, Modern Dance, and Ballet and Modern Dance (double major). School/College Description: The TCU College of Fine Arts is home to six academic units: the School of Art, the School for Classical & Contemporary Dance, the School of Music, the Department of Design, the Department of Fashion Merchandising, and the Department of Theatre. We offer 33 undergraduate degree programs and 24 advanced degree programs to prepare the next generation of creative leaders in the arts. Students in the College of Fine Arts study with renowned professors and guest artists, annually present more than 350 public performances, and regularly present art, design, and research in juried exhibitions and competitions. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Required Application Materials & Application Instructions 1. Cover letter/Letter of Application including the following: teaching philosophy, research/creative activity (2 pages maximum); 2. Curriculum vitae with links to website or professional activity; 3. Contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. All applications will be held in confidence. After the initial review of applications, candidates advancing to the second round of consideration may be asked to submit supporting materials, including evidence of academic and artistic excellence, and research and/or creative work. These may also include evaluations, teaching observations, syllabi, links to a professional activity website, and/or letters of recommendation. All materials are to be submitted online. Questions regarding the application process may be directed to Human Resources at hrtalentacquisition@tcu.edu or 817-257-7790. Other questions may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Suki John, Professor of Dance, at s.john@tcu.edu . Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert c854f986 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) f4326e45 Last Name (required) 056a1079 Email (required) df80e505 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) d9010962 Last Name (required) 5ef6d22c Email (required) e21fd93e Who would you like to share this with? ec8093ed Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 2bbf4e01 Last Name (required) d618f0da Email (required) 47fa20a4 Resume c197cb72 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d4e5fe47 Last Name (required) 407425a0 Email (required) bb5a6ddb What type of job are you looking for? (required) 01ce5fd3 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply accbf2be Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-finance-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Finance", "description": "Assistant Professor of Finance - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Finance - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Finance M.J. Neeley School of Business Apply Now Assistant Professor of Finance 501298 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 17 2026 M.J. Neeley School of Business Application Deadline: 12/31/2026 Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of Finance at Texas Christian University invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Finance (tenure-track) in the Neeley School of Business for Fall 2027 or until filled. Faculty will be expected to produce high-quality research, participate in university service, and deliver high-quality instruction in courses across the School's undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. Applications are welcome from both Ph.D. candidates and current Assistant Professors at other institutions. Current Assistant Professors should demonstrate a strong record of high quality research and teaching and the potential for continued excellence in both areas. The position requires a completed Ph.D. in Finance or a related discipline. The applicant for this position should be capable of effectively teaching finance courses at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. Evidence of teaching effectiveness and strong research capabilities are required. Candidates must be able to communicate clearly both orally and in writing. Department Details: The Department of Finance has 28 full-time faculty members. Finance faculty regularly publish in leading academic journals, including the Journal of Finance, Review of Financial Studies, Journal of Financial Economics, American Economic Review, Journal of Financial and Quantitative Analysis, and Management Science. The LKCM Center for Financial Studies enhances the quality, prestige, and national visibility of finance programs at the Neeley School of Business by providing research support for faculty, databases, industry partnerships, and assisting students searching for excellent employment opportunities in finance. Since 1973 the Neeley School has offered the Educational Investment Fund (EIF), a large endowment run entirely by students, offering them valuable investment experience working with fellow students to manage a portfolio of stocks and bonds. School/College Description: The nationally ranked TCU Neeley School of Business has more than 3,500 students enrolled across undergraduate and graduate programs, with approximately one third of TCU students in its programs as majors, minors or advanced degree seekers. Departments include Accounting, Business Information Systems, Entrepreneurship and Innovation, Finance, Management and Leadership, Marketing and Supply and Value Chain Management, as well as seven graduate programs including full-time, part-time and online MBA and MS degrees. The Neeley School was ranked No. 9 in the nation and No. 1 in Texas for highest starting salaries for undergraduates in 2022 (Poets&Quants, 2022). The school\u2019s BBA is ranked #25 Best Undergraduate program in 2024, and was named one of the top 10 Undergraduate Business Schools to Watch (Poets&Quants, 2022). The Neeley School has the No. 36 ranked Full-time MBA in the U.S., and is No. 8 for Learning, No. 24 for Entrepreneurship, and No. 32 for Networking (Bloomberg Businessweek, 2024). The Neeley School is committed to fostering an inclusive, scholarly community composed of individuals who, through their diverse and sometimes competing perspectives, contribute to a free and intellectually challenging culture where students, faculty, staff and alumni have equitable opportunities and can forge paths toward personal and professional growth. We build upon the momentum generated by living the Neeley Promise: The Neeley School of Business unleashes human potential with leadership at the core and innovation in our spirit. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Applications must include a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Applications must be submitted electronically through the TCU HR system at https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/search. From there, search for \u201cfinance\u201d using the \u201cJob Search\u201d box and use the \u201cApply Now\u201d button to apply for the position of interest. Review of applications will begin immediately. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 841d9ca3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) 579dceda Last Name (required) 29332302 Email (required) 8256b7c7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) b4f16883 Last Name (required) 34f602b9 Email (required) 77a8d141 Who would you like to share this with? 7817a158 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 14d25dda Last Name (required) e2b46aab Email (required) 2830e7b5 Resume b54aeb1e Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 61949a3a Last Name (required) 4527d21a Email (required) 436cf975 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 21ce4739 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 0b950f76 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-management-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Management", "description": "Assistant Professor of Management - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Management - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Management M.J. Neeley School of Business Apply Now Assistant Professor of Management 501150 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Jul 1 2026 M.J. Neeley School of Business Application Deadline: until filled Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of Management and Leadership at Texas Christian University invites applications for an assistant professor tenure-track position in Strategic Management within the Neeley School of Business. Successful candidates will begin employment in Fall 2027. Description Successful candidates will have significant research and teaching accomplishments in strategic management or closely related fields. Primary responsibilities include conducting high-quality research and teaching undergraduate and/or MBA courses. Collegiality and a demonstrated ability to work with others are core values of our department. The teaching load and salary are competitive and commensurate with qualifications. Department Details: Our Department The department provides an exceptional work environment, with highly supportive colleagues who are dedicated to the vision of being world class thought leaders. The tenured/tenure-track faculty include David Allen, Artemis Boulamatsi, Terrance \u201cT.L.\u201d Boyd, Garry Bruton, Michael Cole, Craig Crossland, Lisa Schurer Lambert, Hettie Richardson, Alessandra Rizzi, Abbie Shipp, David Skandera, and Mary Uhl-Bien. Faculty regularly publish in top journals, with publications in recent years in Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Journal of Applied Psychology, Journal of Management, Organization Science, Personnel Psychology, and Strategic Management Journal, among others. Our faculty are editors of top journals in their disciplines, hold leadership positions in the Academy of Management and Strategic Management Society, and serve on editorial boards of the premier journals in management. We are seeking candidates who share our vision and can contribute effectively to our productive and collaborative environment. For information on all of our faculty, see https://neeley.tcu.edu/about/directory/index.php?departments=management--leadership. School/College Description: The nationally ranked TCU Neeley School of Business has more than 3,500 students enrolled across undergraduate and graduate programs, with approximately one third of TCU students in its programs as majors, minors or advanced degree seekers. Departments include Accounting, Business Information Systems, Entrepreneurship and Innovation, Finance, Management and Leadership, Marketing and Supply and Value Chain Management, as well as seven graduate programs including full-time, part-time and online MBA and MS degrees. The Neeley School was ranked No. 9 in the nation and No. 1 in Texas for highest starting salaries for undergraduates in 2022 (Poets&Quants, 2022). The school\u2019s BBA is ranked #25 Best Undergraduate program in 2024, and was named one of the top 10 Undergraduate Business Schools to Watch (Poets&Quants, 2022). The Neeley School has the No. 36 ranked Full-time MBA in the U.S., and is No. 8 for Learning, No. 24 for Entrepreneurship, and No. 32 for Networking (Bloomberg Businessweek, 2024). The Neeley School is committed to fostering an inclusive, scholarly community composed of individuals who, through their diverse and sometimes competing perspectives, contribute to a free and intellectually challenging culture where students, faculty, staff and alumni have equitable opportunities and can forge paths toward personal and professional growth. We build upon the momentum generated by living the Neeley Promise: The Neeley School of Business unleashes human potential with leadership at the core and innovation in our spirit. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Requirements Candidates for the position should possess (or expect completion of by August 2027) an earned doctorate in strategic management or a related field. To Apply All applications must be submitted electronically through the TCU HR system at https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-strategic-management-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states. From this page, you can search for this position by the title \u201cAssistant Professor of Strategic Management.\u201d Alternatively, under \"Category\u201d select \"Neeley Business School\" to find this position among a listing of all business school positions. Applicants should attach the following to the online application: (1) a cover letter, (2) curriculum vita demonstrating research accomplishments, (3) evidence of teaching activity and excellence, and (4) three references with addresses, email addresses, and phone numbers. The search committee is being chaired by Mary Uhl-Bien. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Requests for additional information or assistance should be directed to: Human Resources Talent Acquisition Texas Christian University hrtalentacquisition@tcu.edu 817-257-7790 Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert a46b3aff Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) a2e60629 Last Name (required) d75a90c6 Email (required) c0e898f3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 6e1bb179 Last Name (required) cfefa6dc Email (required) a4880dc1 Who would you like to share this with? 8f6dda8d Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 58bc3fc9 Last Name (required) 1add3ef0 Email (required) a3a66098 Resume c3aa3cf0 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 84d5f6dd Last Name (required) e7747f1c Email (required) 57c58fc1 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 8935c6fb Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply dadacac3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-professional-practice-in-counseling-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-a7b19467-1f70-41e4-80ec-9ace21c4c4af": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in Counseling", "description": "Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in Counseling - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in Counseling - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in Counseling College of Education Apply Now Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in Counseling 501282 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 11 2026 College of Education Application Deadline: Position will be open until filled. Review of Applications will begin October 12, 2026 Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. We are seeking an Assistant Professor of Professional Practice with a demonstrated professional counseling identity, strong teaching and organizational skills, and experience working on CACREP accreditation tasks. The successful candidate will teach and advise students in our CACREP-accredited Clinical Mental Health Counseling master's program and will additionally mentor students in our Counseling & Counselor Education doctoral program (currently seeking CACREP accreditation). Specific duties include: \u2022 Teach graduate counseling courses such as Orientation, Introduction to Helping Skills, Small Group Counseling, Counseling Diverse Populations, Intro to Marriage & Family Therapy, and Play Therapy. \u2022 Serve as the program\u2019s CACREP liaison and coordinate CACREP accreditation efforts (e.g., continuous program evaluation, compliance reports, endorsing candidates for NCC). \u2022 Consult with program faculty and Frog CARE Centers staff to ensure CACREP compliance \u2022 Develop and revise courses, with program faculty, to reflect current field practices and standards. \u2022 Implement innovative teaching practices, such as technology integration, simulations, or case-based learning. \u2022 Advise and mentor graduate students, including serving on oral/comprehensive examination and dissertation committees. \u2022 Provide service to the college, university, and counseling-related professional organizations. \u2022 Contribute to program marketing and recruitment through open houses, information sessions, and community events. Required Qualifications: - Doctorate (Ph.D.) in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program. ABD candidates will be considered, but must complete degree requirements by the appointment date. - Demonstrated excellence or potential for excellence in teaching across the CACREP curriculum. - Evidence of professional engagement in the counseling field. - Knowledge of and ability to coordinate CACREP accreditation compliance. Preferred Qualifications: - Experience as instructor-of-record for graduate counseling courses. - Licensed to practice counseling and eligible for Texas LPC credential. - Two or more years of clinical experience in schools, communities, hospitals, and/or non-profit settings. Department Details: The Department of Counseling, Societal Change & Inquiry (CSCI) is located in TCU\u2019s College of Education and houses the Counseling, Curriculum Studies, and Youth Advocacy and Educational Studies programs. These programs engage students who aim to positively impact society in various ways, including addressing mental health through counseling, examining the relationships between school curricula and society, and working with youth in educational organizations. School/College Description: TCU\u2019s College of Education provides exceptional preparation for the most inspired and inspiring educators, counselors, leaders, and youth advocates. The college offers both B.S. and B.S.E. degrees at the undergraduate level, as well as five master's programs and five doctoral programs, many of which are nationally recognized. Programs include eighteen content area pathways to teacher certification in K -12 education along with programs and/or concentrations in youth advocacy, early intervention, bilingual education, English as a Second Language (ESL), curriculum and instruction, curriculum studies, counseling and counselor education, educational leadership, higher education leadership, science education, mathematics education, language and literacy education, and special education. TCU is the only university in the nation with two on-campus laboratory schools, Starpoint and KinderFrogs, for children with learning differences. Students have the opportunity to engage in real-world experiences with our centers, institutes, programs, and community partners. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Applicants should submit (1) a cover letter indicating their interest and qualifications for this position; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) contact details (name, affiliation, e-mail address, and phone number) for three references. TCU uses an online application protocol administered by Human Resources. All application materials must be submitted electronically at: https://jobs.tcu.edu. For more information, contact Marcella Stark at m.stark@tcu.edu Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 03988d4e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) f647555e Last Name (required) df926710 Email (required) d31f92e8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 8c098a36 Last Name (required) e5bb5247 Email (required) 13c3d68e Who would you like to share this with? ae11e444 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) a296bdce Last Name (required) 1f66f63b Email (required) a92a79a9 Resume e90eb2e2 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 653e96df Last Name (required) a92e60ca Email (required) b4f6c83c What type of job are you looking for? (required) f2427a67 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 72b0caaa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-strategic-communication-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication", "description": "Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication Schieffer College of Communication Apply Now Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication 501318 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 28 2026 Schieffer College of Communication Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on October 21, 2026. Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of Strategic Communication in the Bob Schieffer College of Communication at Texas Christian University (TCU) in Fort Worth, Texas invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates whose research and teaching contribute to the field of strategic communication and expand the department\u2019s strengths. The department has particular interest in candidates with qualitative approaches to strategic communication. We seek candidates whose research contributes to areas of disciplinary relevance and student demand, including: advertising and brand communication; sports communication; social and cultural implications of strategic communication; technology and society; digital, social, and emerging media. Applicants must be able to teach a variety of introductory and upper-level undergraduate and graduate courses in our program, including, for example; introductory advertising or public relations, creative strategy, management, research, global communication, law and/or ethics, campaigns, or other required courses. Candidates may have an interest in creating and teaching new electives. Successful candidates may also benefit from the Schieffer Media Insights Lab, which is the college\u2019s social and digital media research and teaching facility, and have the opportunity to contribute to our college-level PhD in Media and Communication or our postbaccalaureate certificate program in digital and social media analysis. Required qualifications: Ph.D. in a relevant field (e.g., advertising, public relations, strategic communication, communication, marketing, consumer psychology) by the time of appointment; Evidence of research productivity or a developing research agenda with potential for publication in high-impact scholarly outlets in the advertising, public relations, and/or strategic communication disciplines; Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring; Ability to contribute to a collaborative and collegial academic environment. Preferred qualifications: Expertise in strategic communication, including but not limited to brand communication, consumer culture, digital advertising, creative strategy, persuasion, and other related areas; Expertise in qualitative research methodologies, such as in-depth interviewing, ethnography, discourse analysis, netnography, interpretive consumer research, critical-cultural approaches, or mixed-methods designs that incorporate qualitative inquiry; Evidence of a research agenda with relevance to contemporary strategic communication issues affecting consumers, organizations, communities, or society; Related professional experience and strong relationships with strategic communication industries are highly desirable. We seek candidates who are committed to providing undergraduate and graduate students with an active, supportive learning environment, advancing knowledge through theoretically and practically significant scholarship, and contributing to the inclusive excellence of our university community. The teaching load for tenure-stream faculty is 2-3 or 3-2, with course reductions offered in the first year and fourth year to support their progress toward tenure and promotion. Department Details: The Department of Strategic Communication is TCU's home for advertising, public relations, and new media. Through the theories, methods, and practices of strategic communication taught by highly regarded teachers, scholars, and professionals, students learn to create effective, innovative, and responsible stories about brands and organizations, solving real-world communication challenges. The Department of Strategic Communication is one of four departments in the Bob Schieffer College of Communication, housed in the Moudy South Building, and serves more than 400 majors. In addition to state-of-the-art facilities, which include writeable walls, updated classroom and computer technology, and adaptable furniture, the Department of Strategic Communication also has cutting-edge educational experiences from the student-run strategic communication agency, Roxo, to the National Student Advertising Competition (NSAC) and guided internships. School/College Description: In 2023, the Schieffer College celebrated the 10th anniversary of its naming for TCU alumnus and longtime CBS network TV correspondent Bob Schieffer. The college is the academic home for four departments: Communication Studies; Film, Television, and Digital Media; Journalism; and Strategic Communication. Some 1,150 undergraduate student majors complete coursework in areas that include: Advertising and Public Relations; Cinema and Media Studies; Digital and Social Media; Health Communication and Media; Interpersonal and Organizational Communication; Journalism and News Media Studies; and Sports Broadcasting. About 30 graduate students pursue master\u2019s degrees in Communication Studies or Strategic Communication, and some 60 full-time and 15 part-time faculty teach in the college. The college\u2019s award-winning student experiential learning activities include print, video, and digital news media, a speech and debate team, an advertising and public relations agency, a radio station, and sports broadcasting productions. The college also offers a number of off-campus study options to students. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Applications must include a cover letter that addresses the position requirements, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and a list of three academic references with current contact information included. Applications must be submitted electronically through the TCU HR system. Letters of recommendation will be requested from your three references at a later stage in the process. Your references will receive an email from TCU asking them to upload their LOR on your behalf. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert c33348c7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) 6a725c36 Last Name (required) 65e23dfc Email (required) d8b25f9b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) f78ede83 Last Name (required) 13a34ddc Email (required) e2ce8f96 Who would you like to share this with? 6413dc13 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 8eeb0879 Last Name (required) 852a1eeb Email (required) 59433c93 Resume cff0b9ec Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 61fbd388 Last Name (required) 925b8ed1 Email (required) a84284d6 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 110867d4 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 68fd076c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-professsor-of-english-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professsor of English", "description": "Assistant Professsor of English - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant Professsor of English - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professsor of English AddRan College Apply Now Assistant Professsor of English 501311 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 23 2026 Closing on: Nov 10 2026 AddRan College Application Deadline: November 10, 2026 Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of English at Texas Christian University (TCU) invites applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant professor rank with a focus in law and literature and a scholarly specialization in any period within either pre-1950 American literature or post-1900 British and/or Irish literature. We seek a colleague whose work will contribute to growing pre-law programs in the English department, with opportunities to participate in a developing pre-law institute in the AddRan College of Liberal Arts. Tenure line faculty have a regular 3/2 course load, and newly hired faculty receive pre-tenure course release support for research. All tenure-line faculty teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, mentor undergraduate and graduate M.A. and Ph D theses/dissertations, and serve on graduate student committees. Candidates with relevant expertise may also contribute to our department\u2019s programs in Comparative Race and Ethnic Studies and Women and Gender Studies as well as the program in Digital Culture/Data Analytics and other interdisciplinary initiatives. The position carries a nationally competitive salary, benefits, and internal research support. Department Details: As the largest department in the AddRan College of Liberal Arts, the TCU Department of English is a vibrant and diverse intellectual community. We offer distinct majors and minors in the study of writing and rhetorics; literatures and cultures; and creative writing as well as an MA in English (including an Accelerated BA to MA program), a PhD in English, a PhD in Rhetoric and Composition, and a pilot postdoctoral program. We also serve as the administrative home for the programs in Women and Gender Studies and Comparative Race and Ethnic Studies. Our 35 full-time permanent faculty members are dedicated teacher-scholars and productive leaders in their fields. The department values and supports synergistic inquiry between the areas of study represented within the department as well as interdisciplinary connections across the university. Learn more about us at https://addran.tcu.edu/english/ School/College Description: Named for TCU\u2019s founders, Addison and Randolph Clark, the AddRan College of Liberal Arts is home to the core academic disciplines of the humanities and social sciences. The College includes approximately 155 full-time faculty members, 10 departments (Criminology & Criminal Justice, Economics, English, Geography, History, Philosophy, Political Science, Religion, Sociology & Anthropology, and World Languages & Global Studies ), and two units of Reserve Officers\u2019 Training Corps (Army and Air Force). AddRan College departments confer 17 Bachelor of Arts and 7 Bachelor of Science degrees, a Bachelor of General Studies, an online master\u2019s degree in Criminology and Criminal Justice, a Master of Liberal Arts degree, and master\u2019s and Ph.D. degrees in History, English, and Rhetoric and Composition. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Required qualifications: A PhD in English or a relevant discipline in hand at the time of appointment, an excellent track-record in research, and demonstrated teaching excellence at the college level. Review of materials begins November 10, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Required materials must be submitted to TCU\u2019s online application: \u25cf CV \u25cf Letter of application outlining research and teaching interests and ability to contribute to pre-law programs \u25cf 2- to 3-page abstract of dissertation or book project \u25cf Writing sample Additional materials will be requested after first-round review: three letters of recommendation and unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert e7e6eec5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) 0bd60d5b Last Name (required) 46d95270 Email (required) b268db87 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 3bee6180 Last Name (required) 9b0b3841 Email (required) 6a6ed987 Who would you like to share this with? 714ce75e Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) c689b30a Last Name (required) c6b0eb49 Email (required) 1a1cd3ca Resume 9c8d1d1f Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4312fbe1 Last Name (required) cbec553f Email (required) c734ccf3 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 163555e5 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply d0dfd39c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-in-mathematics-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor in Mathematics", "description": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor in Mathematics - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant, Associate or Full Professor in Mathematics - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant, Associate or Full Professor in Mathematics College of Science & Engineering Apply Now Assistant, Associate or Full Professor in Mathematics 501285 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 18 2026 College of Science & Engineering Application Deadline: November 1, 2026 (soft deadline) Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of Mathematics at Texas Christian University (TCU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning in August 2027. Preference will be given to candidates in areas of active research in the department, which include Geometry, Topology, Operator Algebras, Number Theory, Representation Theory of Lie Groups, and Statistics/Data Science. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Mathematics, Statistics, or a closely related field by August 2027. Exceptional candidates may be considered for appointment at a higher rank. Department Details: The Department of Mathematics is a small, collegial unit, currently with 21 full-time faculty members. The department serves approximately 125 majors in Math, Actuarial Science, and Data Science and has a small graduate program offering Master\u2019s and Doctoral degrees in Mathematics. The university is located within the Dallas-Fort Worth metroplex, a vibrant metropolitan area of about 8.5 million people. School/College Description: The Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering encompasses 9 departments (Biology, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Computer Science, Engineering, Environmental and Geological Sciences, Mathematics, Nutritional Sciences, Physics & Astronomy, and Psychology) as well as the Ranch Management Program, which offers both an undergraduate degree and a one-year certificate program. Davis College is also home to the Pre-Health Professions Institute, the Karyn Purvis Institute for Child Development, the Institute of Behavioral Research, the Institute for Environmental Studies, Monnig Meteorite Gallery, and the Institute for Ranch Management. Davis College is the second largest at TCU in terms of both undergraduate enrollment and number of majors. It contains a disproportionate percentage of high-achieving students, as evidenced by the fact that almost one-half of the students in the Honors College have majors in The Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering. Research opportunities abound for undergraduates, with 46 percent of majors engaging in a substantive experience during which they work one-on-one with their faculty mentor. Davis College also has five doctoral programs and 16 master\u2019s programs, as well as two graduate certificate programs. Davis College faculty are true teacher-scholars, for whom instruction and research are viewed as complementary activities. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Candidates should apply through MathJobs (http://www.mathjobs.org/) and must also submit information through the TCU HR system. For the application on MathJobs, please submit (a) an AMS cover sheet; (b) a cover letter; (c) a complete vita, including a list of publications; (d) a research plan; (e) a teaching statement specifically addressing your teaching style, classroom techniques, and assessment strategies; (f) copies of graduate transcripts; (g) three or more confidential letters of recommendation, at least one of which addresses the candidate\u2019s teaching in detail; and (h) for applicants who have not yet completed a Ph.D., undergraduate transcripts. Candidates are strongly encouraged to describe in their application materials how they might support the university and department priorities described above. The posting in the TCU HR system can be found at https://jobs.tcu.edu/ . Here, candidates will fill out a brief application form and upload their vita. This site also contains further information about TCU, the Davis College of Science and Engineering, and Fort Worth. Applicants who have not submitted the required documents at both sites will not be considered. Applicants who submit all materials by November 1, 2026, are guaranteed full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 949bb185 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) 4c4e012d Last Name (required) 7854ce16 Email (required) 52db6113 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 7c6970f0 Last Name (required) 6e7b4464 Email (required) 4df1e810 Who would you like to share this with? a751fe1c Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 92271548 Last Name (required) 85665c1b Email (required) 1c67a1f3 Resume 3d74aabb Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b6739a4c Last Name (required) 898200f8 Email (required) 88bb313f What type of job are you looking for? (required) 9349da15 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 0a25903d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-of-chemistry-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Chemistry", "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Chemistry - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Chemistry - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Chemistry College of Science & Engineering Apply Now Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Chemistry 501167 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Jul 7 2026 College of Science & Engineering Application Deadline: Open Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry is conducting an open search for a tenure-track or tenured position in chemistry or aligned fields adopting a molecular perspective. While candidates from any subdiscipline are encouraged to apply, emphasis will be placed on individuals with backgrounds in inorganic or bioinorganic chemistry. Department Details: The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry subscribes to TCU's teacher-scholar model wherein undergraduate education is linked to a productive, externally funded research enterprise. The department offers undergraduate degrees in chemistry and biochemistry as well as M.S. and Ph.D. degrees. School/College Description: The Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering encompasses 9 departments (Biology, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Computer Science, Engineering, Environmental and Geological Sciences, Mathematics, Nutritional Sciences, Physics & Astronomy, and Psychology) as well as the Ranch Management Program, which offers both an undergraduate degree and a one-year certificate program. Davis College is also home to the Pre-Health Professions Institute, the Karyn Purvis Institute for Child Development, the Institute of Behavioral Research, the Institute for Environmental Studies, Monnig Meteorite Gallery, and the Institute for Ranch Management. Davis College is the second largest at TCU in terms of both undergraduate enrollment and number of majors. It contains a disproportionate percentage of high-achieving students, as evidenced by the fact that almost one-half of the students in the Honors College have majors in The Louise Dilworth Davis College of Science & Engineering. Research opportunities abound for undergraduates, with 46 percent of majors engaging in a substantive experience during which they work one-on-one with their faculty mentor. Davis College also has five doctoral programs and 16 master\u2019s programs, as well as two graduate certificate programs. Davis College faculty are true teacher-scholars, for whom instruction and research are viewed as complementary activities. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: Candidates should submit a letter of interest, cv, statement of teaching philosophy (1 page), and description of proposed research (3-5 pages). Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 8aa3b363 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) 189b7fd2 Last Name (required) d7a6f2db Email (required) 9713b3ce Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 39010afe Last Name (required) 66fbb259 Email (required) d0af5e64 Who would you like to share this with? 06188ead Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 5a752151 Last Name (required) 8c54eb6a Email (required) 76748ce6 Resume a8d604a9 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) a16a8948 Last Name (required) 7641a356 Email (required) 8b843cea What type of job are you looking for? (required) 5819e501 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply fc5101cf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-or-assistant-associate-professor-of-professional-practice-occupational-therapy-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-cd6dc3bf-6d7b-4315-b6d0-d42763b2be27": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Professional Practice - Occupational Therapy", "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Professional Practice - Occupational Therapy - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Professional Practice - Occupational Therapy - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Professional Practice - Occupational Therapy Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences Apply Now Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Professional Practice - Occupational Therapy 501297 Faculty Full-time Opening on: Sep 18 2026 Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences Application Deadline: Open Until filled Position Details: This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences invites applications for one 12-month faculty position as a Tenure-Track Assistant/Associate Professor OR Assistant/Associate Professor of Professional Practice (non-tenure) for the developing entry-level Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) Program at Texas Christian University (TCU). Tenure-Track Faculty Qualifications: Successful applicants will have strong written and interpersonal communication skills, the ability to maintain an active research/scholarship agenda (including extramural funding) and teaching proficiency within their area of expertise supporting the developing entry-level Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) Program at Texas Christian University (TCU). Professional Practice Track Faculty Qualifications: Successful applicants will have strong written and interpersonal communication skills and teaching proficiency within their area of expertise in support of the developing entry-level Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) Program at Texas Christian University (TCU). Other responsibilities include advising and mentoring graduate students and contributing to university and community service in alignment with institutional missions. Applicants must be licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the State of Texas and have earned a Doctoral degree (OTD, PhD, EdD or equivalent) with three years clinical experience preferred. Those with advanced clinical credentialing/expertise (E.g., geriatrics, neuro-rehabilitation, hand therapy, etc.) are especially encouraged to apply. Salary and rank will be commensurate with the qualifications and experience of the candidate. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This position is slated to begin June 1, 2027. Applications not submitted online will not be considered. Questions about the position can be directed via email (OTSearch@tcu.edu) to: Leah Samantha Randolph, PhD, OTR, Search Chair - Assistant Professor. Department Details: The Department of Occupational Therapy at Texas Christian University is committed to preparing practice-scholars through a collaborative, student-centered learning environment. Faculty work closely together in a culture that values mentorship, interprofessional engagement, and a strong scholarship agenda that informs teaching, research and clinical practice. Through small, single-cohort class structures, students and faculty develop meaningful relationships that foster individualized support, active collaboration, and a cohesive \u201cfamily\u201d culture within the program. Consistent with the core values of Texas Christian University\u2014Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence\u2014the department emphasizes ethical leadership, active participation in scholarship and service, and a deep commitment to student success. Faculty are dedicated to advancing the profession through innovative teaching, impactful research, and community partnerships while cultivating graduates who are prepared to lead with compassion, professionalism, and a commitment to excellence in occupational therapy practice. School/College Description: The Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences consists of programs that prepare future health care and human services professionals. The academic units within Harris College \u2013 Applied Health Sciences, Communication Sciences & Disorders, Occupational Therapy, Kinesiology, Nurse Anesthesia, Nursing, and Social Work \u2013 are home to 1,900 students who are supported by committed and talented faculty and staff. Harris College supports the mission, vision, and values of TCU; we prepare global citizens to think and practice as ethical leaders in health care and educational settings. Harris College offers 20 degree pathways in our health-related disciplines. Students benefit from learning experiences in campus laboratories and hospitals, clinics, schools, fitness facilities, and community service agencies throughout the Dallas-Fort Worth Area. On campus, the Miller Speech & Hearing Clinic provides services for more than 300 families each year and serves as a professional practice site for students majoring in speech pathology and habilitation of the deaf. TCU Nursing and the School of Nurse Anesthesia provide innovative learning experiences in their state-of-the-art simulation centers. The faculty and students at Harris College actively engage in research for the purpose of improving health and well-being. Undergraduate and graduate students have opportunities to form mentoring relationships with internationally recognized faculty as they conduct studies in such areas as pharmacogenetics, carbohydrate metabolism, exercise physiology, health disparities, heart disease, aging, Parkinson\u2019s disease, caregiving, language development in children with hearing loss, and forgiveness among others. Our graduates are competent, compassionate, and in demand in the workforce. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: To apply, submit Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Teaching Statement and contact information for three references online at https://jobs.tcu.edu/en-us/listing/ (select \"Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences\" to locate the position announcement). For tenure-track applicants, please include a Research Statement with agenda. References will not be contacted without prior notification of candidates. All questions regarding the application process should be directed to Human Resources at hrtalent@tcu.edu. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 1c0e1c54 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full-time Full-time First Name (required) e04157e6 Last Name (required) 1c8117ee Email (required) f75346e3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 34950d44 Last Name (required) 0d0b9111 Email (required) 0a1cfe6f Who would you like to share this with? df1a2e00 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) c14184c3 Last Name (required) d70657ba Email (required) b9e3a4bc Resume 5141c726 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) a46faaad Last Name (required) f5395ad0 Email (required) b3a18ec6 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 31ab2631 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 61721eb8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/biology-faculty-adjunct-pool-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-33d24c37-9ae4-444e-829c-13ae147325c0": {"title": "Biology Faculty Adjunct Pool", "description": "Biology Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Biology Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Biology Faculty Adjunct Pool College of Science & Engineering Apply Now Biology Faculty Adjunct Pool 499446 Adjunct Faculty Temporary Opening on: Apr 1 2024 College of Science & Engineering Application Deadline: Not applicable Position Details: The Department of Biology in the College of Science & Engineering occasionally has openings for part-time temporary adjunct instructors. Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in biology would add the applicant to a pool which is available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. Department Details: N/A School/College Description: The TCU College of Science & Engineering (CSE) encompasses 10 departments (Biology, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Computer Science, Engineering, Environmental Sciences, Geological Sciences, Mathematics, Nutritional Sciences, Physics & Astronomy, and Psychology) as well the Ranch Management Program, which offers both an undergraduate degree and a one-year certificate program. The College is also home to the Pre-Health Professions Institute, the Karyn Purvis Institute for Child Development, the Institute of Behavioral Research, and the Institute for Ranch Management. The College is the second largest at TCU in terms of both undergraduate enrollment and number of majors. CSE contains a disproportionate percentage of high achieving students, as evidenced by the fact that almost one-half the students in the Honors College have majors in the College of Science & Engineering. Research opportunities abound for undergraduates, with over 40 percent of majors engaging in a substantive experience during which they work one-on-one with their faculty mentor. The College also has five doctoral programs and 16 master\u2019s programs as well as two graduate certificate programs. The College faculty are true teacher-scholars, for whom instruction and research are viewed as complementary activities. University & Fort Worth Description: ABOUT TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University sits on 302 acres nestled in a primarily residential part of Fort Worth, just minutes away from downtown. The University includes seven schools and colleges, in addition to the John V. Roach Honors College and the Burnett School of Medicine. Currently, TCU enrolls more than 10,200 undergraduates and 1,700 graduate students. Twenty-eight percent of students self-identify as a member of a minority group, five percent are international students, and forty-five percent are from out-of-state. Our students are supported by more than 2,200 faculty and staff. The University has more than 700 full-time faculty members and is a top 100 National University as classified by US News and World Report and has a Carnegie Classification of R2: Doctoral Universities \u2013 High Research Activity. ABOUT FORT WORTH Like TCU, Fort Worth has the approachable, friendly charm of a smaller town, but offers the amenities, cultural activities, diversity and unique personality of a much larger city. Fort Worth, Texas, is the 13th largest city in the United States with an ever-growing population nearing 1 million. Fort Worth and TCU have grown together in a nearly 150-year relationship. You\u2019ll find that many Horned Frogs remain here after graduation, thanks to the region\u2019s thriving job market. Fort Worth is part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area, the fourth largest metropolitan area in the United States, and the number 1 tourist destination in Texas. In 2018, bizjournals.com ranked Fort Worth the 7th most affordable city to live and work in the United States and U.S. News and World Report named Fort Worth one of the Best Places to Live. Fort Worth, Dallas and Arlington all rank among the top 25 most diverse cities in the country. Fort Worth is known for its vast array of cultural, educational and entertainment opportunities. The city boasts three world class art museums\u2014the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall is one of the premier performance venues in the country. Concerts, film festivals and other events are held regularly at Sundance Square, Panther Island and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: TCU only accepts online applications and documents. To apply for a part-time adjunct position, attach a letter of application and a curriculum vitae to the online application. Additional documents may be required by the department at a later time. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 4b55e723 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Temporary Temporary First Name (required) 03e43228 Last Name (required) 67e285c1 Email (required) 63ac607c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 3069a3f5 Last Name (required) e4be0a5f Email (required) 7b70dc9f Who would you like to share this with? 54a87838 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to