Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 3474a4de Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Temporary Temporary First Name (required) f37c489c Last Name (required) 3a8c4ca1 Email (required) bf62fcd2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) eaaf353d Last Name (required) d5d26700 Email (required) 4532c27e Who would you like to share this with? 153506e6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 1bca260c Last Name (required) 64ec09d9 Email (required) e0269a29 Resume 216c3d89 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 1797af6f Last Name (required) 2b3218cd Email (required) 8e00fb30 What type of job are you looking for? (required) f46ee98d Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 08fff181 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait..