ew, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) dd94479f Last Name (required) 53fcd906 Email (required) 60faf00c Resume 5d114aec Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) eb5ef864 Last Name (required) 9eab3842 Email (required) 6afb2273 What type of job are you looking for? (required) 425981f8 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply a7bcaaef Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to custom