Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/statistics-faculty-adjunct-pool-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-7be838ce-456c-431e-84a9-451daab455e9": {"title": "Statistics Faculty Adjunct Pool", "description": "Statistics Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Statistics Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Statistics Faculty Adjunct Pool M.J. Neeley School of Business Apply Now Statistics Faculty Adjunct Pool 499514 Adjunct Faculty Temporary Opening on: Apr 10 2024 M.J. Neeley School of Business Application Deadline: Not applicable Position Details: The Department of Information Systems & Supply Chain Management (INSC) in the Neeley School of Business occasionally has openings for part-time temporary adjunct instructors of business statistics. This may involve undergraduate and/or graduate statistics/analytics classes. Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in INSC would add the applicant to a pool which is available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. Department Details: N/A School/College Description: The nationally ranked TCU Neeley School of Business has approximately 3,000 students enrolled across undergraduate and graduate programs, with approximately one third of TCU students in its programs as majors, minors or advanced degree seekers. Departments include Accounting, Business Information Systems, Entrepreneurship and Innovation, Finance, Management and Leadership, Marketing and Supply and Value Chain Management, as well as seven graduate programs including full-time, part-time and online MBA and MS degrees. The Neeley School was ranked #9 in the nation and #1 in Texas for highest starting salaries for undergraduates in 2022 (Poets&Quants). The school\u2019s BBA is ranked #21 Best Undergraduate program in 2023, and was named one of the top 10 Undergraduate Business Schools to Watch in 2022 (Poets&Quants). The Neeley School has the #4 ranked full-time MBA in Texas in 2022 (Bloomberg Businessweek) and the #32 MBA in the World in 2022 (Wall Street Journal/Time Higher Education). The Neeley School is committed to fostering an inclusive, scholarly community composed of individuals who, through their diverse and sometimes competing perspectives, contribute to a free and intellectually challenging culture where students, faculty, staff and alumni have equitable opportunities and can forge paths toward personal and professional growth. We build upon the momentum generated by living the Neeley Promise: The Neeley School of Business unleashes human potential with leadership at the core and innovation in our spirit. University & Fort Worth Description: ABOUT TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University sits on 302 acres nestled in a primarily residential part of Fort Worth, just minutes away from downtown. The University includes seven schools and colleges, in addition to the John V. Roach Honors College and the Burnett School of Medicine. Currently, TCU enrolls more than 10,200 undergraduates and 1,700 graduate students. Twenty-eight percent of students self-identify as a member of a minority group, five percent are international students, and forty-five percent are from out-of-state. Our students are supported by more than 2,200 faculty and staff. The University has more than 700 full-time faculty members and is a top 100 National University as classified by US News and World Report and has a Carnegie Classification of R2: Doctoral Universities \u2013 High Research Activity. ABOUT FORT WORTH Like TCU, Fort Worth has the approachable, friendly charm of a smaller town, but offers the amenities, cultural activities, diversity and unique personality of a much larger city. Fort Worth, Texas, is the 13th largest city in the United States with an ever-growing population nearing 1 million. Fort Worth and TCU have grown together in a nearly 150-year relationship. You\u2019ll find that many Horned Frogs remain here after graduation, thanks to the region\u2019s thriving job market. Fort Worth is part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area, the fourth largest metropolitan area in the United States, and the number 1 tourist destination in Texas. In 2018, bizjournals.com ranked Fort Worth the 7th most affordable city to live and work in the United States and U.S. News and World Report named Fort Worth one of the Best Places to Live. Fort Worth, Dallas and Arlington all rank among the top 25 most diverse cities in the country. Fort Worth is known for its vast array of cultural, educational and entertainment opportunities. The city boasts three world class art museums\u2014the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall is one of the premier performance venues in the country. Concerts, film festivals and other events are held regularly at Sundance Square, Panther Island and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: TCU only accepts online applications and documents. To apply for a part-time adjunct position, attach a letter of application and a curriculum vita to the online application. Additional documents may be required by the department at a later time. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert ed9a2168 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Temporary Temporary First Name (required) 4af658d6 Last Name (required) 6fb6b619 Email (required) 2e01125f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 943f6a3a Last Name (required) d778cc33 Email (required) 5fb73243 Who would you like to share this with? 0dc331f2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) cfcefe26 Last Name (required) 231b7524 Email (required) bf33104e Resume d470ff03 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 73ba3c59 Last Name (required) 3e83361a Email (required) d2522018 What type of job are you looking for? (required) ef39b9f9 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 080e8688 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/strategic-communication-faculty-adjunct-pool-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-f6c34150-70aa-4002-8933-f7c302a4afec": {"title": "Strategic Communication Faculty Adjunct Pool", "description": "Strategic Communication Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Strategic Communication Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Strategic Communication Faculty Adjunct Pool Schieffer College of Communication Apply Now Strategic Communication Faculty Adjunct Pool 499425 Adjunct Faculty Temporary Opening on: Apr 1 2024 Schieffer College of Communication Application Deadline: Not applicable Position Details: The Department of Strategic Communication in the Bob Schieffer College of Communication occasionally has openings for part-time temporary adjunct instructors. Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in strategic communication would add the applicant to a pool which is available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. Department Details: N/A School/College Description: In 2023, the Schieffer College celebrates the 10th anniversary of its naming for TCU alumnus and longtime CBS network TV correspondent Bob Schieffer. The college is the academic home for four departments: Communication Studies; Film, Television and Digital Media; Journalism; and Strategic Communication. Some 1,250 undergraduate student majors complete coursework in areas that include: Advertising and Public Relations; Cinema and Media Studies; Digital and Social Media; Health Communication and Media; Interpersonal and Organizational Communication; Journalism and News Media Studies; and Sports Broadcasting. About 30 graduate students pursue master\u2019s degrees in Communication Studies or Strategic Communication, and some 60 full-time and 15 part-time faculty teach in the college. The college\u2019s award-winning student experiential learning activities include print, video and digital news media, a speech and debate team, an advertising and public relations agency, a radio station, and sports broadcasting productions. The college also offers a number of off-campus study options to students. University & Fort Worth Description: ABOUT TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University sits on 302 acres nestled in a primarily residential part of Fort Worth, just minutes away from downtown. The University includes seven schools and colleges, in addition to the John V. Roach Honors College and the Burnett School of Medicine. Currently, TCU enrolls more than 10,200 undergraduates and 1,700 graduate students. Twenty-eight percent of students self-identify as a member of a minority group, five percent are international students, and forty-five percent are from out-of-state. Our students are supported by more than 2,200 faculty and staff. The University has more than 700 full-time faculty members and is a top 100 National University as classified by US News and World Report and has a Carnegie Classification of R2: Doctoral Universities \u2013 High Research Activity. ABOUT FORT WORTH Like TCU, Fort Worth has the approachable, friendly charm of a smaller town, but offers the amenities, cultural activities, diversity and unique personality of a much larger city. Fort Worth, Texas, is the 13th largest city in the United States with an ever-growing population nearing 1 million. Fort Worth and TCU have grown together in a nearly 150-year relationship. You\u2019ll find that many Horned Frogs remain here after graduation, thanks to the region\u2019s thriving job market. Fort Worth is part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area, the fourth largest metropolitan area in the United States, and the number 1 tourist destination in Texas. In 2018, bizjournals.com ranked Fort Worth the 7th most affordable city to live and work in the United States and U.S. News and World Report named Fort Worth one of the Best Places to Live. Fort Worth, Dallas and Arlington all rank among the top 25 most diverse cities in the country. Fort Worth is known for its vast array of cultural, educational and entertainment opportunities. The city boasts three world class art museums\u2014the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall is one of the premier performance venues in the country. Concerts, film festivals and other events are held regularly at Sundance Square, Panther Island and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: TCU only accepts online applications and documents. To apply for a part-time adjunct position, attach a letter of application and a curriculum vita to the online application. Additional documents may be required by the department at a later time. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 9be6085f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Temporary Temporary First Name (required) fdc80b71 Last Name (required) f407b654 Email (required) 8718485c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) f1946e84 Last Name (required) 0fc3b542 Email (required) c349977c Who would you like to share this with? 30af9448 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) c67c4b55 Last Name (required) 059b7574 Email (required) 08395099 Resume 04d1c4ab Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 216e27dd Last Name (required) 25c2a5c4 Email (required) 6782af2b What type of job are you looking for? (required) 98407ada Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 80b4ff80 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/string-music-education-faculty-adjunct-pool-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states": {"title": "String Music Education Faculty Adjunct Pool", "description": "String Music Education Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States String Music Education Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode String Music Education Faculty Adjunct Pool College of Fine Arts Apply Now String Music Education Faculty Adjunct Pool 499699 Adjunct Faculty Temporary Opening on: Jul 2 2024 College of Fine Arts Application Deadline: Not applicable Position Details: The School of Music in the College of Fine Arts occasionally has openings for part-time temporary adjunct instructors in string music education. Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in music would add the applicant to a pool which is available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. Minimum qualifications: \u2022 Master\u2019s Degree or higher in Music Education or Music, with teacher certification (current or previous) \u2022 Primary instrument/high performance skill on a string instrument (violin, viola, cello, or bass). \u2022 Three years of successful EC-12 music teaching experience in strings/orchestra classes. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 At least five years of successful EC-12 music teaching experience \u2022 Expertise in traditional and contemporary approaches to strings teaching \u2022 Experience mentoring preservice teachers and/or student teacher supervision. \u2022 Successful teaching experience at the College/University level Essential Functions: \u2022 Teach undergraduate courses in string techniques for instrumental music education and composition majors. \u2022 Teach Junior-level Instrumental Methods and Materials (strings) course. \u2022 Mentor preservice teachers in preparation for and during student teaching. Department Details: N/A School/College Description: The TCU College of Fine Arts is home to six academic units: the School of Art, the School for Classical & Contemporary Dance, the School of Music, the Department of Design, the Department of Fashion Merchandising, and the Department of Theatre. The college is comprised of approximately 1000 students and offers 33 undergraduate degree programs and 24 advanced degree programs to prepare the next generation of creative leaders in the arts. Students in the College of Fine Arts study with renowned professors and guest artists, annually present more than 350 public performances and display art, design, and research in juried exhibitions and competitions. The college also offers a minor and certificate in Arts Leadership & Entrepreneurship and oversees two on-campus art galleries. University & Fort Worth Description: ABOUT TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University sits on 302 acres nestled in a primarily residential part of Fort Worth, just minutes away from downtown. The University includes seven schools and colleges, in addition to the John V. Roach Honors College and the Burnett School of Medicine. Currently, TCU enrolls more than 10,200 undergraduates and 1,700 graduate students. Twenty-eight percent of students self-identify as a member of a minority group, five percent are international students, and forty-five percent are from out-of-state. Our students are supported by more than 2,200 faculty and staff. The University has more than 700 full-time faculty members and is a top 100 National University as classified by US News and World Report and has a Carnegie Classification of R2: Doctoral Universities \u2013 High Research Activity. ABOUT FORT WORTH Like TCU, Fort Worth has the approachable, friendly charm of a smaller town, but offers the amenities, cultural activities, diversity and unique personality of a much larger city. Fort Worth, Texas, is the 13th largest city in the United States with an ever-growing population nearing 1 million. Fort Worth and TCU have grown together in a nearly 150-year relationship. You\u2019ll find that many Horned Frogs remain here after graduation, thanks to the region\u2019s thriving job market. Fort Worth is part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area, the fourth largest metropolitan area in the United States, and the number 1 tourist destination in Texas. In 2018, bizjournals.com ranked Fort Worth the 7th most affordable city to live and work in the United States and U.S. News and World Report named Fort Worth one of the Best Places to Live. Fort Worth, Dallas and Arlington all rank among the top 25 most diverse cities in the country. Fort Worth is known for its vast array of cultural, educational and entertainment opportunities. The city boasts three world class art museums\u2014the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall is one of the premier performance venues in the country. Concerts, film festivals and other events are held regularly at Sundance Square, Panther Island and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: TCU only accepts online applications and documents. To apply for a part-time adjunct position, attach a letter of application describing your relevant qualifications for the position, including a brief statement of teaching philosophy, and a curriculum vita to the online application. Please add the names and contact information of three references to either your letter of application or CV. Additional documents may be required by the department at a later time. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert b63d2f28 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Temporary Temporary First Name (required) 76aae414 Last Name (required) 5934c1ad Email (required) 4ba1de24 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) dc95fe64 Last Name (required) 5637dde1 Email (required) 18d4f7cd Who would you like to share this with? 95c5a427 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) cf6c9e1a Last Name (required) 5aa0e3da Email (required) 06ef30ea Resume dedc3e88 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) f6acc6a5 Last Name (required) 3913b145 Email (required) b50bb17d What type of job are you looking for? (required) d8e139a2 Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply fc227fd6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/student-physician-coach-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-999dd6c8-7c46-4ca2-9c86-4c2d25f72b40": {"title": "Student Physician Coach", "description": "Student Physician Coach - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Student Physician Coach - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Student Physician Coach Burnett School of Medicine Apply Now Student Physician Coach 501338 Faculty Part-time Opening on: Oct 8 2026 Burnett School of Medicine Position Details: The Student Physician Coach will be assigned a group of students to oversee throughout their medical school curriculum and will be responsible for monitoring academic and professionalism progression, coaching students through professional identity formation, helping them navigate academic challenges, and developing them as empathetic scholars. The Student Physician Coach plays a critical role in overseeing students\u2019 progression through the Longitudinal Integrated Clerkship (LIC), ensuring that, across the clerkships, students meet the expected milestones and learning objectives for each clerkship. The Student Physician Coach educates and tracks student professionalism, fosters professional identity formation, supports academic progress, and supports the wellness of each assigned student. Student Physician Coaches ensure comprehensive achievement of all clerkship objectives, recognize strengths, and identify areas for improvement to optimally foster professional identity development. Duties and Essential Job Functions: Works with the Director of Student Physician Coaching to ensure long-term success with their student cohort. Tracks progression and professionalism development for their cohort of students. Collaborates with the Director of Student Physician Coaching, Clerkship Directors, and faculty preceptors to ensure optimal communication about student performance across all curricular activities. Provides guidance for their cohort of medical students, supporting their professional and personal development throughout the four-year curriculum; Regularly monitors their students\u2019 progress and self-reflection on competency milestones, guides students in individual learning planning, and meets with their students individually and in small groups. Individual meetings occur at least quarterly with each student. Attends weekly group coaching meetings. Conferences with students in incidents of not meeting curricular and/ or professionalism expectations, provides constructive feedback, and assists students in identifying appropriate resources for self-improvement and support. Refers students to Learning Specialists, Career Advisors, Mental Health counseling, or other individuals as needed. Reviews faculty narratives of student assessment for areas of possible improved performance and provides suggestions for improvement; Encourages and supports each student as an individual by creating an environment of professionalism, respect, tolerance, and acceptance. Serves on School of Medicine committees as assigned; Performs additional duties as assigned. Required Education and Experience: MD or DO Must qualify for Assistant Professor rank or above at the Burnett School of Medicine Required Licensure/Certification/Specialized Training: Physicians with active clinical practice must have and maintain an unrestricted license to practice medicine Physicians with active clinical practice must have current ABMS (American Board of Medical Specialties) Certification in their area of chosen specialty Preferred Education and Experience: Understanding of educational pedagogy as it relates to the clinical sciences Experience managing professionals in a complex organization Proven experience in management of multiple initiatives and multiple sites Experience with LCME and/or other accrediting bodies Experience working with diverse students or diverse populations Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Excellent interpersonal and communication skills Excellent clinical skills Track record of teaching excellence, educational leadership, and organizational talent Commitment to cultural diversity and equal opportunity Experience in working with and developing faculty Experience in giving and receiving feedback Commitment to delivery of patient-centered medicine Physical Requirements (With or Without Accommodations): Visual acuity to read information from computer screens, forms, and other printed materials and information. Able to speak (enunciate) clearly in conversation and general communication. Hearing ability for verbal communication/conversation/responses via telephone, telephone systems, and face-to-face interactions. Manual dexterity for typing, writing, standing and reaching, flexibility, body movement for bending, crouching, walking, kneeling and prolonged sitting. Lifting and moving objects and equipment up to 10 lbs. Work Environment: Work is indoors and sedentary and is subject to schedule changes and/or variable work hours. There are no harmful environmental conditions present for this job. The noise level in this work environment is usually moderate. Traveling between multiple work sites is often necessary. This role is an in-person and on-campus. SCHOOL/COLLEGE DESCRIPTION The Anne Burnett Marion School of Medicine at Texas Christian University, Fort Worth\u2019s M.D. school, opened with a class of 60 students in July 2019. The School of Medicine\u2019s focus on communication, a first-of-its-kind curriculum and the development of Empathetic Scholars\u2122 uniquely positions the organization to radically transform medical education, improving care for future generations. University & Fort Worth Description: About TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University is a world-class, private, Carnegie-classified national research university located in Fort Worth, Texas. Inspired by its mission and core values of integrity, engagement, community, and excellence, TCU consistently ranks among the top universities and colleges in the United States. TCU\u2019s campus \u2014 regularly ranked among the nation\u2019s most beautiful \u2014 spans 302 acres in a primarily residential area just minutes from downtown. The university comprises nine schools and colleges offering 117 areas of undergraduate study, 62 master\u2019s level programs, and 37 areas of doctoral study. TCU is a leader across several disciplines, including health care, business, energy, and the arts. Total enrollment stands at 12,980, including 11,152 undergraduates and 1,828 graduate students. Students are supported by over 2,200 faculty and staff, including more than 700 full-time faculty members. About Fort Worth Fort Worth blends the approachable charm of a smaller city with the amenities, cultural energy, and distinctive personality of a major metro. As the nation\u2019s 11th-largest city, with a rapidly growing population of more than 1 million, Fort Worth and TCU share a relationship that spans more than a century \u2014 one that continues to deepen as many Horned Frogs choose to stay after graduation, drawn by the region\u2019s thriving job market. Part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area \u2014 the nation\u2019s fourth-largest and a top tourism destination \u2014 Fort Worth earned recognition from U.S. News & World Report in 2025 as the No. 4 best big city to live in the United States. Fort Worth offers an impressive array of cultural, educational, and entertainment opportunities, anchored by three world-class art museums \u2014 the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth, and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall stands as one of the premier performance venues in the country. Throughout the year, residents and visitors alike enjoy concerts, film festivals, and other cultural events at Sundance Square, Dickies Arena, Panther Island, and Near Southside venues. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community, and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert e48575e4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Part-time Part-time First Name (required) a3b8f17b Last Name (required) 90f7d618 Email (required) c47ab5b6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 5c7da2d2 Last Name (required) 8e0d365a Email (required) c33457e2 Who would you like to share this with? 8af27664 Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports Frog Camp, Frogs First, on-going first-year student programs and parent/family programs. Administrative Program Specialist Enrollment Management The Administrative Program Specialist is responsible for providing program support by facilitating program goals and objectives. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 9757ce37 Last Name (required) 8efcf8b9 Email (required) 6992fa93 Resume 512b3c95 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Hey! Before you hop away, take the leap and register for Job Alerts! First Name (required) f49205a5 Last Name (required) 2dbab02c Email (required) 418747eb What type of job are you looking for? (required) 9ea0405e Faculty Staff Other Opportunities Job Alert - Select all that apply 633d7a03 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VC/Provost Academic Affairs VC/Provost Academic Affairs Locations TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Take the leap! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in a career at TCU! Close Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/studio-art-faculty-adjunct-pool-tcu-main-campus-texas-united-states-84c6ff0c-b71d-4b2e-b34c-d6086e55e0fd": {"title": "Studio Art Faculty Adjunct Pool", "description": "Studio Art Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Studio Art Faculty Adjunct Pool - TCU Main Campus, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Studio Art Faculty Adjunct Pool College of Fine Arts Apply Now Studio Art Faculty Adjunct Pool 499439 Adjunct Faculty Temporary Opening on: Apr 1 2024 College of Fine Arts Application Deadline: Not applicable Position Details: The Department of Studio Art in the College of Fine Arts occasionally has openings for part-time temporary adjunct instructors. Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in studio art would add the applicant to a pool which is available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. Department Details: N/A School/College Description: The TCU College of Fine Arts is home to six academic units: the School of Art, the School for Classical & Contemporary Dance, the School of Music, the Department of Design, the Department of Fashion Merchandising, and the Department of Theatre. The college is comprised of approximately 1000 students and offers 33 undergraduate degree programs and 24 advanced degree programs to prepare the next generation of creative leaders in the arts. Students in the College of Fine Arts study with renowned professors and guest artists, annually present more than 350 public performances and display art, design, and research in juried exhibitions and competitions. The college also offers a minor and certificate in Arts Leadership & Entrepreneurship and oversees two on-campus art galleries. University & Fort Worth Description: ABOUT TCU Founded in 1873, Texas Christian University sits on 302 acres nestled in a primarily residential part of Fort Worth, just minutes away from downtown. The University includes seven schools and colleges, in addition to the John V. Roach Honors College and the Burnett School of Medicine. Currently, TCU enrolls more than 10,200 undergraduates and 1,700 graduate students. Twenty-eight percent of students self-identify as a member of a minority group, five percent are international students, and forty-five percent are from out-of-state. Our students are supported by more than 2,200 faculty and staff. The University has more than 700 full-time faculty members and is a top 100 National University as classified by US News and World Report and has a Carnegie Classification of R2: Doctoral Universities \u2013 High Research Activity. ABOUT FORT WORTH Like TCU, Fort Worth has the approachable, friendly charm of a smaller town, but offers the amenities, cultural activities, diversity and unique personality of a much larger city. Fort Worth, Texas, is the 13th largest city in the United States with an ever-growing population nearing 1 million. Fort Worth and TCU have grown together in a nearly 150-year relationship. You\u2019ll find that many Horned Frogs remain here after graduation, thanks to the region\u2019s thriving job market. Fort Worth is part of the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area, the fourth largest metropolitan area in the United States, and the number 1 tourist destination in Texas. In 2018, bizjournals.com ranked Fort Worth the 7th most affordable city to live and work in the United States and U.S. News and World Report named Fort Worth one of the Best Places to Live. Fort Worth, Dallas and Arlington all rank among the top 25 most diverse cities in the country. Fort Worth is known for its vast array of cultural, educational and entertainment opportunities. The city boasts three world class art museums\u2014the Kimbell Art Museum, the Modern Art Museum of Fort Worth and the Amon Carter Museum of American Art. The Bass Performance Hall is one of the premier performance venues in the country. Concerts, film festivals and other events are held regularly at Sundance Square, Panther Island and Near Southside venues. Required Application Materials & Application Instructions: TCU only accepts online applications and documents. To apply for a part-time adjunct position, attach a letter of application and a curriculum vita to the online application. Additional documents may be required by the department at a later time. Employment Values Statement: Texas Christian University values Integrity, Engagement, Community and Excellence in the workplace. TCU treats applicants and employees with fairness and respect. TCU hires and promotes individuals based on their qualifications and their commitment to making a positive impact on our student-centered community. TCU is an equal opportunity employer and follows all applicable employment laws. TCU fairly considers all qualified individuals, ensuring we are a workplace free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. TCU Annual Security Report & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Texas Christian University is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own safety and security. TCU\u2019s Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy & Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and the Higher Education Opportunity Act. This report includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings owned or controlled by the University, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The statements of policy contained within this report address institutional policies, procedures, and programs concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, emergency notifications and timely warning of crimes, sexual and interpersonal violence, and personal safety at TCU. Additionally, this report outlines fire safety systems, policies and procedures for on-campus housing facilities, as well as residence hall fire statistics. The Annual Security Report and Fire Safety Report can be found on the TCU Police Department website at https://police.tcu.edu/annual-security-report , or a paper copy of the report may be obtained by contacting the TCU Police Department at 817-257-7930, or via email at police@tcu.edu . Sign Up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 5031825b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Temporary Temporary First Name (required) 78e4d8df Last Name (required) aa75b599 Email (required) 7df02da7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 15fc65e5 Last Name (required) a3fcd561 Email (required) b3b24e85 Who would you like to share this with? 17ceea3c Send Please wait... Done Not You? We've sent an email! Recently Posted Jobs Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations Finance & Administration The Assistant Director of Contract Administration Operations provides contract-related guidance from a business perspective and support to the entire TCU community through all phases of contract negotiation, preparation and execution. Performs a wide range of duties related to contracts including review, revision and preparation of contracts that comply with Texas Christian University policies and procedures in advance of final review and signature. Coordinator of New Student & Family Programs Student Affairs The Coordinator, New Student & Family Programs, is responsible for collaboration with university departments to execute First Year Leadership Opportunities (FLO), service to first-year commuter students and assistance with Orientation for all incoming undergraduate students. The position also supports